## DESCRIPTION
##   Identifying Vectors in a Plane
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by nhamblet

## DBsubject(Geometry)
## DBchapter(Vector geometry)
## DBsection(Planes)
## Date(8/23/07)
## Institution(Union College)
## Level(3)
## KEYWORDS('Vector', 'Plane')

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',        'PGML.pl',
    'parserVectorUtils.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context("Vector");

#  The vectors u and v

do {
    $U = non_zero_vector3D(-3, 3);
    $V = non_zero_vector3D(-3, 3);
    $N = $U x $V;
} until norm($N) != 0;

#  Some vectors in the plane
@W = (2 * $U + $V, -$U + 2 * $V, -3 * $V);
# and some other random ones.
push(@W, non_zero_vector3D(-3, 3)) for (1 .. 3);

@shuffle = random_subset(4, 0 .. $#W);

@dd = map { DropDownTF(@W[$_] . $N == 0 ? 'T' : 'F') } @shuffle;

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

BEGIN_PGML

The two vectors [`\vec{u} = [$U]`] and [`\vec{v} = [$V]`]
determine a plane in space.  Determine if the following vector are in the same plane as [`\vec{u}`] and [`v`] (true) or not (false). 

a) [``[$W[$shuffle[0]]]``] [_]{$dd[0]}

b) [``[$W[$shuffle[1]]]``] [_]{$dd[1]}

c) [``[$W[$shuffle[2]]]``] [_]{$dd[2]}

d) [``[$W[$shuffle[3]]]``] [_]{$dd[3]}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
How does [`\vec{u} \times \vec{v}`] compare to the other vectors in the plane?
END_PGML_HINT

ENDDOCUMENT();
